--- A function copied per signature is scanned in its own scope, as the
--- function itself is: its first assignment to a name is a local of its
--- own, and inside a package's copy the program's names are invisible.
--- The copy of llm's `act` made for the second tool list had read the
--- program's `one` — the record the first call answered — as the loop's
--- own local `one` (a schema's text), and refused the package's own push
--- onto its list in both modes. (The model's address answers nobody: each
--- call's failure is the same value in both modes.)
use llm

--- the current weather in a city
fn weather[city]
    return 'sunny in `upper[city]`'

--- the population of a city, in millions
fn population[city]
    return '`upper[city]`: 0.5 million'

m = llm.reach['openai://127.0.0.1:9/self-model']
one = llm.act[m, llm.ask['How warm is it in Lisbon?'], tools = [weather]]
two = llm.act[m, llm.ask['Which is larger, Lisbon or Porto?'], tools = [weather, population]]
log[one.ok]
log[one.kind]
log[two.ok]
log[starts[two.reason, 'cannot reach the model']]
